{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788371004512,"sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_75eec4ccc1144f9696ef54fd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs","newString":"Type::Float => format!(\"tl_float({value})\"),","oldString":"Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n@@ -436,9 +436,9 @@\n Type::Char => unreachable!(\"Char cannot reach the printer, refused by the checker\"),\n Type::Str => format!(\"tl_quote({value})\"),\n Type::Sink => unreachable!(\"a sink only ever prints raw, never through the printer\"),\n Type::Int | Type::Int64 => format!(\"str({value})\"),\n-Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n+Type::Float => format!(\"tl_float({value})\"),\n Type::Bool => format!(\"(\\\"true\\\" if {value} else \\\"false\\\")\"),\n Type::Vec(elem) => {\n     let e = format!(\"e{depth}\");\n     format!(\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n@@ -436,9 +436,9 @@\n Type::Char => unreachable!(\"Char cannot reach the printer, refused by the checker\"),\n Type::Str => format!(\"tl_quote({value})\"),\n Type::Sink => unreachable!(\"a sink only ever prints raw, never through the printer\"),\n Type::Int | Type::Int64 => format!(\"str({value})\"),\n-Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n+Type::Float => format!(\"tl_float({value})\"),\n Type::Bool => format!(\"(\\\"true\\\" if {value} else \\\"false\\\")\"),\n Type::Vec(elem) => {\n     let e = format!(\"e{depth}\");\n     format!(\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_py.rs","time":{"start":1788371004510,"end":1788371004511}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The helper block looks correct. Now I need to make the actual emit changes:\n\n1. `show`: `Type::Float` arm → `format!(\"tl_float({value})\")`.\n2. `expr`: `Kind::Float(n)` → `crate::float::lit(*n)`.\n3. `arith`: add Float branch.\n4. `emit` helper inclusion: add the two new entries.\n\nLet me also reconsider the doc comments I wrote — they're a bit rambly. Per AGENTS.md, comments should be concise and explain the why. My doc comments on the helpers are longish but they do explain real subtleties (the repr boundary differences, signed zero). Hmm, but some lines are filler (\"The `a ==  ́0` test catching both zero signs...\"). Let me tighten later. Actually let me simplify the comments to be cleaner. The FLOAT_HELPER comment: explain it reshapes Python's repr into JS String(number) form, and the two deltas (E ranges + `.0` + exponent padding). The DIVF comment: Python raises ZeroDivisionError; IEEE says Infinity/NaN; signed zero via `<`. Let me rewrite those comment blocks shorter. I'll do that after the functional edits. \n\nFirst functional edits.\n\nEdit for show (lineodor  ́374):\noldString: `        Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),`\nnewString: `        Type::Float => format!(\"tl_float({value})\"),`\n\nEdit for expr (lineodor  ́426):\noldString: `        Kind::Float(_) => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),`\nnewString: `        Kind::Float(n) => crate::float::lit(*n),`\n\nEdit for arith (lineodor  ́770-778):\noldString:\n```\nfn arith(ty: &Type, op: BinOp, l: String, r: String) -> String {\n    if *ty == Type::Int64 {\n```\nnewString:\n```\nfn arith(ty: &Type, op: BinOp, l: String, r: String) -> String {\n    if *ty == Type::Float {\n        // IEEE binary64 is the type itself (ADR 0007), so plain Python operators are the\n        // exact arithmetic,with no wrap to spell. Python's `/` raises on a zero divisor,so\n        // division spells the IEEE answer through `tl_divf` instead of a plain `/`.\n        match op {\n            BinOp::Add => format!(\"({l} + {r})\"),\n            BinOp::Sub => format!(\"({l} - {r})\"),\n            BinOp::Mul => format!(\"({l} * {r})\"),\n            BinOp::Div => format!(\"tl_divf({l}, {r})\"),\n            other => unreachable!(\"{other} is not arithmetic\"),\n        }\n    } else if *ty == Type::Int64 {\n```\n\nEdit for the helper inclusion (lineodor  ́272-274):\noldString:\n```\n        (arith64 || uses(\"tl_i64(\") || uses(\"tl_sum64(\"], I64_HELPER),\n        (arith, ARITH_HELPER),\n        (arith64, ARITH64_HELPER),\n```\nnewString:\n```\n        (arith64 || uses(\"tl_i64(\") || uses(\"tl_sum64(\"], I64_HELPER),\n        (arith, ARITH_HELPER),\n        (arith64, ARITH64_HELPER),\n        (uses(\"tl_float(\"], FLOAT_HELPER),\n        (uses(\"tl_divf(\"], DIVF_HELPER),\n```\n\nLet me apply these edits. Careful with parens at EOL: Rust lines end with `),` or `;` — safe.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06337ec39001X9koU8RYDPGPJh","sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","messageID":"msg_06337be63001y1fU74O1zbOkIa"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788371004516,"sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_eea8cc7598494cbea0049892","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs","newString":"Kind::Float(n) => crate::float::lit(*n),","oldString":"Kind::Float(_) => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n@@ -488,9 +488,9 @@\n fn expr(enums: &Enums, t: &Tir) -> String {\n     match &t.kind {\n         Kind::Str(s) => py_string(s),\n         Kind::Int(n) => n.to_string(),\n-        Kind::Float(_) => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n+        Kind::Float(n) => crate::float::lit(*n),\n         Kind::Var(name) => user(name),\n         Kind::Local(id) => local(*id),\n         Kind::Input => INPUT.to_string(),\n         Kind::Inputs => INPUTS.to_string(),\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n@@ -488,9 +488,9 @@\n fn expr(enums: &Enums, t: &Tir) -> String {\n     match &t.kind {\n         Kind::Str(s) => py_string(s),\n         Kind::Int(n) => n.to_string(),\n-        Kind::Float(_) => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n+        Kind::Float(n) => crate::float::lit(*n),\n         Kind::Var(name) => user(name),\n         Kind::Local(id) => local(*id),\n         Kind::Input => INPUT.to_string(),\n         Kind::Inputs => INPUTS.to_string(),\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_py.rs","time":{"start":1788371004514,"end":1788371004516}},"id":"prt_06337ec45001iEXNJ6D7OzDfc2","sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","messageID":"msg_06337be63001y1fU74O1zbOkIa"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788371004520,"sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_e385d64ac7394647917944a0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs","newString":"fn arith(ty: &Type, op: BinOp, l: String, r: String) -> String {\n    if *ty == Type::Float {\n        // IEEE binary64 is the type itself (ADR 0007), so plain Python operators are the\n        // exact arithmetic,with no wrap to spell. Python's `/` raises on a zero divisor,so\n        // division spells the IEEE answer through `tl_divf` instead of a plain `/`.\n        match op {\n            BinOp::Add => format!(\"({l} + {r})\"),\n            BinOp::Sub => format!(\"({l} - {r})\"),\n            BinOp::Mul => format!(\"({l} * {r})\"),\n            BinOp::Div => format!(\"tl_divf({l}, {r})\"),\n            other => unreachable!(\"{other} is not arithmetic\"),\n        }\n    } else if *ty == Type::Int64 {","oldString":"fn arith(ty: &Type, op: BinOp, l: String, r: String) -> String {\n    if *ty == Type::Int64 {"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n@@ -833,10 +833,21 @@\n \n /// One arithmetic expression at the width the node's type names (kantord/toylang#83): the\n /// same emulation either way, through the 64-bit helpers when the type says so.\n fn arith(ty: &Type, op: BinOp, l: String, r: String) -> String {\n-    if *ty == Type::Int64 {\n+    if *ty == Type::Float {\n+        // IEEE binary64 is the type itself (ADR 0007), so plain Python operators are the\n+        // exact arithmetic,with no wrap to spell. Python's `/` raises on a zero divisor,so\n+        // division spells the IEEE answer through `tl_divf` instead of a plain `/`.\n         match op {\n+            BinOp::Add => format!(\"({l} + {r})\"),\n+            BinOp::Sub => format!(\"({l} - {r})\"),\n+            BinOp::Mul => format!(\"({l} * {r})\"),\n+            BinOp::Div => format!(\"tl_divf({l}, {r})\"),\n+            other => unreachable!(\"{other} is not arithmetic\"),\n+        }\n+    } else if *ty == Type::Int64 {\n+        match op {\n             BinOp::Div => format!(\"tl_div64({l}, {r})\"),\n             BinOp::Rem => format!(\"tl_rem64({l}, {r})\"),\n             BinOp::Add => format!(\"tl_i64({l} + {r})\"),\n             BinOp::Sub => format!(\"tl_i64({l} - {r})\"),\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs\n@@ -833,10 +833,21 @@\n \n /// One arithmetic expression at the width the node's type names (kantord/toylang#83): the\n /// same emulation either way, through the 64-bit helpers when the type says so.\n fn arith(ty: &Type, op: BinOp, l: String, r: String) -> String {\n-    if *ty == Type::Int64 {\n+    if *ty == Type::Float {\n+        // IEEE binary64 is the type itself (ADR 0007), so plain Python operators are the\n+        // exact arithmetic,with no wrap to spell. Python's `/` raises on a zero divisor,so\n+        // division spells the IEEE answer through `tl_divf` instead of a plain `/`.\n         match op {\n+            BinOp::Add => format!(\"({l} + {r})\"),\n+            BinOp::Sub => format!(\"({l} - {r})\"),\n+            BinOp::Mul => format!(\"({l} * {r})\"),\n+            BinOp::Div => format!(\"tl_divf({l}, {r})\"),\n+            other => unreachable!(\"{other} is not arithmetic\"),\n+        }\n+    } else if *ty == Type::Int64 {\n+        match op {\n             BinOp::Div => format!(\"tl_div64({l}, {r})\"),\n             BinOp::Rem => format!(\"tl_rem64({l}, {r})\"),\n             BinOp::Add => format!(\"tl_i64({l} + {r})\"),\n             BinOp::Sub => format!(\"tl_i64({l} - {r})\"),\n","additions":12,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_py.rs","time":{"start":1788371004518,"end":1788371004519}},"id":"prt_06337ec4c001Hlhp4662WfEylH","sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","messageID":"msg_06337be63001y1fU74O1zbOkIa"}}
