{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788371038540,"sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_5008f4a76310449a99f5d75c","state":{"status":"error","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-float-build-python/src/emit_py.rs","newString":"/// Python's `/` on floats raises ZeroDivisionError where IEEE 754 division by zero returns\n/// Infinity (ADR 0007, the Q37 ruling[],), so a Float division spells the zero case\n/// through here. The result's sign is the signs' XOR, IEEE's rule, read with `<` rather than\n/// `==` because `-0.0` is a reachable value (`-0.0` is a literal)and `-0.0 < 0`\n/// tells its sign where equality cannot. `0 / 0` is NaN, the IEEE answer, the way JS's\n/// `/` gives it (kantord/toylang#149).","oldString":"/// Python's `/` on floats raises ZeroDivisionError where IEEE division by zero returns Infinity\n/// (ADR 0007,ther Q37 ruling[], so a Float division spells the zero case through here. The\n/// result's sign is the signs' XOR, IEEE's rule, which is why zero is tested with `<` rather\n/// than equality: `-0.0` is a real value a Float can hold (`-0.0` is a literal it\n/// parses as),and a zero divisor's sign flips the quotient's.\n\n\n/// `float(\"-inf\")` writes the negative zero's natural sign counterpart;the conditional is what\n/// picks which infinity,with `a` and `b`'s signs compared rather than tested for equality so a\n/// signed zero divisor works. \n\n/// The `a == 0` test catching both zero signs is what makes `0.0 / 0.0` NaN,\n/// IEEE's answer,ther same way JS's `/` gives it (kantord/toylang#149)."},"error":"Could not find oldString in the file. It must match exactly, including whitespace, indentation, and line endings.","time":{"start":1788371038528,"end":1788371038538}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The current DIVF comment block is lines  ́117-128. My oldString differed (I had `ruling[],` but file has `ruling`). Let me redo with exact text.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06338713c001kQJbiq5z8dpZCu","sessionID":"ses_f9cd2b4c5ffeW0f5SqvVxijLH6","messageID":"msg_0633862140012mlAIM2XFDiFv5"}}
